          "kind": "quality",
          "severity": "FLAG",
          "criterion": "c-6",
          "text": "TestReviewSectionSameLengthOrder compares strings.Index results without checking either id is present: if `t-2` were missing from the body (Index -1) the test would still pass. Asserting both indexes are \u003e= 0 would make it a real check.",
          "resolution": "non-blocking, left"
        },
        {
          "round": 1,
          "kind": "quality",
          "severity": "NOTE",
          "criterion": "c-6",
          "text": "If the tie-break were removed outright rather than reversed, the order of two same-length ids would follow Go's random map iteration, so TestReviewSectionSameLengthOrder would catch that mutant only about half the time. A reversed comparison is caught every time.",
          "resolution": "non-blocking, left"
        },
        {
          "round": 1,
          "kind": "quality",
          "severity": "FLAG",
          "criterion": "c-6",
          "text": "TestReviewSectionClipsAtRuneStart's failure message slices body[strings.Index(body, \"## Reviewer\"):], which panics if the heading is absent. That only happens on the failure path, and the test still fails, but the panic hides the real diagnostic.",
          "resolution": "non-blocking, left"
        },
        {
          "round": 1,
          "kind": "quality",
          "severity": "NOTE",
          "criterion": "c-1",
          "text": "TestRecorderContextRebuildFailures reaches both 'could not be rebuilt' arms: the missing spec through ContextScope and the malformed gates.toml through the BuildContext secrets error.",
          "resolution": "non-blocking, left"
        },
        {
          "round": 2,
          "kind": "quality",
          "severity": "NOTE",
          "text": "TestReviewSectionSameLengthOrder relies on map iteration for its input order, so a mutant that drops the same-length tie-break comparator entirely may survive intermittently; reversing it (the contract's case) is caught deterministically",
          "resolution": "non-blocking, left"
        }
      ]
    }
